WEBVTT

NOTE The homepage film to 0:55.99, then the organisations extension. Timings measured off FILM04-audio-master-v5.mp3 and vo-org.mp3.

1
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:05.700
Yeah.

2
00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:07.130
We hate Mondays.

3
00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:08.630
Tuesdays too.

4
00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:09.300
But…

5
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.920
…what if it's your nervous system.

6
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.600
When our nervous systems are unregulated,

7
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.720
sometimes we're the last to find out.

8
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.380
But everyone else around us can see it.

9
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.450
By the time we realize it,

10
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:21.960
we've ruined another moment.

11
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.160
That's why SafeRise is here.

12
00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.200
Our protocols help you harness Attention,

13
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.800
Awareness, and Authorship…

14
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:33.200
…whether it's anger, anxiety, overwhelm,

15
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.420
resentment, or burnout.

16
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.300
Personal, in relationships, or at work.

17
00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.560
Built for the state you're actually in.

18
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:45.500
We even have your physical substrates

19
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:49.160
covered…

20
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.550
Because when you're overwhelmed…

21
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.640
you don't want to be the last to find out.

22
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.220
That's one person.

23
00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:59.390
But as a people manager,

24
00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.120
you're responsible for many more.

25
00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.490
Some are trained in leadership, communications,

26
00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.440
with high competence.

27
00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.590
But you've seen pressure change what they can reach

28
00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.240
in the tough moments.

29
00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.210
And you've seen where it lands.

30
00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.510
The mistake nobody can explain.

31
00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:15.050
The sick day that isn't.

32
00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.020
The good one who starts looking to leave.

33
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.010
That's not a training problem.

34
00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.690
SafeRise offers a way back to the capability

35
00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.850
beneath every skill they've trained.

36
00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.360
Scoped to the industry and to their role.

37
00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.090
Not just the state they're in —

38
00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:31.370
the room, the decision, the shift they have to finish.

39
00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:35.310
Offer full organization access to SafeRise from day one.

40
00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.250
Now that's people management, at scale.

41
00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.220
SafeRise… let's enjoy Mondays again.
